{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-355387",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n- ${min}_{x\\in B}k(x)$ is the smallest output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in B}k(x)$ is an input in $B$ where that smallest output occurs.\n\nThe output values are $-5,$ $-8,$ $-2,$ and $-8,$ so the minimum output value is $-8.$ This minimum occurs at both $x=-2$ and $x=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{min}_{x\\in B}k(x)=-8\\,\\text{and}\\,\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in B}k(x)=\\{-2,3\\}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
